@startuml
title Bounded end-to-end engineering orchestration
actor Operator
participant Controller
participant "Recovery / Design" as Design
participant "Existing Scheduler" as Scheduler
participant "Quality" as QA
participant "Delivery" as Delivery
Operator -> Controller: plan (default dry-run)
Controller -> Design: inspect facts and eligible scope
Design --> Controller: explanation, diagrams, approval subjects
Controller --> Operator: exact checkpoint
Operator -> Design: authenticated requirement/design decisions
Operator -> Controller: continue exact persisted run
Controller -> Scheduler: approved plan and granted bounded executions
Scheduler --> Controller: structured verified child evidence
Controller -> QA: independent validation
alt Permitted repair and remaining budget
 QA --> Controller: failure classification
 Controller -> QA: prepare remediation
 Controller -> Scheduler: granted repair task
 Controller -> QA: revalidate
end
Controller -> Delivery: manifest from accepted output identities
Delivery --> Operator: separate publication checkpoint
Operator -> Delivery: authenticated privileged authorization if desired
Controller -> Delivery: bounded authorized observation/operation
Delivery --> Controller: PR / CI / review facts and blockers
Controller --> Operator: report with formal completion separately verified
@enduml
